Report whether dyld ever asks the kernel to map the shared region (enchilada instrument).

launchd is refused twice by shared_region_check_np with ENOMEM, which means the task owns a
shared region whose sr_first_mapping is still -1: no mapping was ever established. Every
failure branch behind shared_region_map_and_slide_2_np reports through SHARED_REGION_TRACE_ERROR,
and shared_region_trace_level is already ERROR, so a refused map would be visible in the log.
Nothing of the kind appears, so the question is whether the call is reached at all.

These printfs answer it. map_and_slide_2 fires when dyld asks for the mapping and records the
file and mapping counts; setup reports the error of shared_region_map_and_slide_setup; enter
reports the shared region it looked up for the process root; first mapping reports the address
that finally becomes sr_first_mapping. They are diagnostics only: no return value, no state and
no policy changes, and each line is prefixed NATIVE_SR so it can be filtered out of a boot log.

